The three measurable spin components are represented by Hermitian operators $\sigma_x,\qquad \sigma_y,\qquad \sigma_z.$ The analyzer experiments already supplied their possible values and their definite-value states: $\begin{array}{c|c|c}
\text{observable}&\text{eigenvalue }+1&\text{eigenvalue }-1\\ \hline
\sigma_z&\ket{u}&\ket{d}\\
\sigma_x&\ket{r}&\ket{l}\\
\sigma_y&\ket{\mathrm{in}}&\ket{\mathrm{out}}
\end{array}$ This information is enough to reconstruct the operators as matrices.

